/*
  Localizable.strings (en)
  VigilUI — base localisation.

  Keys ARE the English text, which is the SwiftUI convention for a base localisation: a
  missing key falls back to the key itself, so English renders correctly whether or not this
  file is present. It exists for two reasons.

  1. It is the file a translator starts from. ru.lproj is this file with the values replaced,
     key for key and section for section, so that the two can be read side by side.
  2. Without at least one real (non-dotfile) resource, SwiftPM emits an EMPTY resource bundle
     with no Info.plist, and codesign then refuses it outright:
       Vigil_VigilUI.bundle: bundle format unrecognized, invalid, or unsuitable
     That failure stopped the very first Mac build at the signing step. A directory holding
     only .placeholder is invisible to SwiftPM, because it skips dotfiles.

  75 keys, covering every LocalizedStringKey in Sources/VigilUI.

  Format specifiers are the ones SwiftUI's LocalizedStringKey interpolation emits, and they
  are part of the key: a String interpolates as %@ and an Int as %lld. Getting one wrong
  does not mistranslate a sentence, it feeds String(format:) the wrong argument size.

  Count-bearing keys are NOT here. They live in Localizable.stringsdict, because English
  cannot say "1 frames" and Russian needs one/few/many plus other where English needs
  one/other. A key must appear in exactly one of the two tables, never both.
*/

